//RS /// The method jobs of one struct or enum: its own methods, then the methods
//RS /// of its nested trait impls. Trait impls nested in a type are real method
//RS /// bodies too. They inherit the type's generic parameters, just as the Rust
//RS /// impl emitted for them does, so those parameters are exposed to the body
//RS /// checker while the parsed method signature is kept for codegen.
